  "title": "Vezf1 loss produces a compact thalamic Hr/Prkcg/Kcnc1/Rasa4-down and Tle2/Abi2-up signature",
  "status": "grounded",
  "rejection_reason": null,
  "exact_observed_result": "Vezf1 generated FDR-supported Rasa4, Prkcg, Kcnc1, and Hr down-regulation with Tle2 and Abi2 up-regulation primarily in 151 TH Prkcd Grin2c Glut; Ctcf and Dnmt3a did not recapitulate the signature, while Zbtb7a showed only modest inverse structure.",
  "biological_interpretation": "Neuronal Vezf1 loss drives a targeted thalamic chromatin/zinc-finger state rather than replaying published endothelial or DNA-methylation mechanisms.",
